# Rust build output
/target

# The vendored Rust registry — the CARGO_HOME this machine's builds are pointed at.
# `export CARGO_HOME="$(pwd)/.cargo-home"` is MANDATORY here, because the default `~/.cargo` fails EACCES
# (a permission fault in the environment, not a project defect); the directory is the crates.io cache and
# the extracted crate SOURCES that path resolves against.
#
# IT IS NEVER A DELIVERABLE AND NEVER A SOURCE: 24 MB and 1,589 files of third-party Rust imports
# (`registry/cache`, `registry/src`, `registry/index`), rebuilt by any fetch. A `git add -A` would sweep all
# of it in -- the same defect the `archive/` and backup-tree rules below exist to prevent, and the reason
# the rule is written HERE beside the other Rust build output rather than at the top of the file.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS OWED TO A FRESH CLONE: `Cargo.lock` STAYS UNCOMMITTED by decision
# (`binding-crate-and-abi.md §1` — pinning a consumer's transitive versions is a consuming-application
# decision), so a cold build FETCHES (`command-sites-and-residue.md §2`: the binding crate's commands fetch;
# the store's carry `--offline`). An ignored registry is therefore consistent with the declared model rather
# than a cache a consumer needs.
.cargo-home/

# Archival (the process rule: archive/ is GITIGNORED)
archive/

# A role's in-flight backup directory. Backup trees for a re-flow pass belong OUTSIDE the
# repository or under the gitignored archive/ -- never in the tree, because a `git add -A`
# in another pass's commit sweeps them in and a backup tree is not a project artifact.
.reflow-backup/

# Another role's in-flight backup directory. Same rule as above: a backup tree belongs
# outside the repository or under the gitignored archive/, never in the tree.
.impl-rc8-backup/

# The supervisor's own in-flight tracker backup, same rule as the others.
.tracker-reflow-backup/

# Generated npm cache (the LIVE/INSTALL battery installs into scratch/live/)
.npm-cache/

# The live battery's copy-drive (a duplicate of the checkout's own files, rebuilt by the report's own commands)
scratch/live/install-0.2.0/drive/
scratch/probe-shape-a/

# The codec wave's depth/number measurement probe (a scratch byproduct, never a deliverable).
# `docs/defects.md` . `DEF-2026-10-21-W` names it as gitignored; it was NOT, so a `git add -A`
# in a later pass would have swept it in. The same rule as the entries above: never a source.
scratch/depth-probe/

# Gate-6/10 archival staging (scratch verification byproducts, never deliverables)
scratch/g7-cache/
scratch/g7-consumer/
scratch/g7-logs/
scratch/g7-stage/

# The type-check fixture's package resolution (`DEF-2026-10-16-Q`; `npm run typecheck`).
# `tsc` refuses a symlinked package under Node10 resolution, so the shipped manifest and the shipped
# declaration are COPIED here by the script from their ONE home in `bindings/js/` -- never edited, never a
# second source of truth -- and the copy must never be committed.
typecheck/node_modules/

# Ephemeral npm cache used by the instrument passes (never a deliverable)
scratch/npmcache/

# The 2026-10-25 DEF-2026-10-20-F landing's measurement byproducts (never deliverables).
# `scratch/def-f-live/` is the assembled-toggle drive that produced
# `docs/specs/storeroom-held-listener-identity-live-report.md`; `scratch/def-f-probe/` is the
# five-consequence probe and the in-memory route bridge that proved the walk cell's `commitFile`
# row was the only thing left red. Same rule as the entries above: a scratch is never a source,
# and `docs/pending.md`'s `G-14` pointer plus `docs/defects.md`'s closure name the drive, so a
# `git add -A` in a later pass must not sweep them in.
scratch/def-f-live/
scratch/def-f-probe/

# The `U-STOREROOM-JSON-CROSSING` gate-11 rounds' measurement byproducts (never deliverables).
# `scratch/jcx-impl/` and `scratch/jcx-s17/` hold the implementation probes and the §17 live
# re-drive's staging; their RESULTS live in the committed specs, test cells and live report.
scratch/jcx-impl/
scratch/jcx-s17/

